<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.9.4: Solving More Quadratic Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02238</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.9.4: Solving More Quadratic Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>dc8a4048-0f0f-4533-9425-9a8d70879d60</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>Solve each equation by rewriting it in <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">factored form</term> and using the <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">zero product property</term>. Be prepared to explain your reasoning.</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(x^2+ 12x + 11 = 0\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the solution to the equation.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> \(x=-1\) and \(x=-11\)</para>
    <para>The equation \(x^2 + 12x + 11 = 0\) can be written as \((x + 11)(x + 1) = 0\), which means \(x + 11 = 0\) or \(x + 1 = 0\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(x^2− 3 = 1\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the solution to the equation.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> \(x=-2\) and \(x=2\)</para>
    <para>The equation \(x^2− 3 = 1\) can be written as \(x^2 − 4 = 0\), which is \((x + 2)(x − 2) = 0\), which means \(x + 2 = 0\) or \(x − 2 = 0\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(x^2− 6x + 7 = -2\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the solution to the equation.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> \(x=3\)</para>
    <para>The equation \(x^2− 6x + 7 = -2\) can be written as \(x^2− 6x + 9 = 0\), which is \((x − 3)(x − 3) = 0\), which means \(x − 3 = 0\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
